# Hotfix propagation chain, most-stable FIRST. THIS FILE DOES NOTHING.
# Copy it to .claude/hotfix-chain at a git root to arm .claude/hooks/hotfix.mjs
# for that repo (platform tier).
#
# After every turn the hook carries each branch into the next one down, but
# only commits whose subject starts with `hotfix:` / `hotfix(scope):` /
# `hotfix!:`. A fix made on release reaches every branch below it without a
# cherry-pick, and nothing else moves.
#
# It never touches a working tree: it merges with `git merge-tree --write-tree`
# and moves the branch ref directly. A branch that is CHECKED OUT anywhere
# (your main checkout, a feature worktree) is not moved behind that checkout's
# back — the hook stops there and tells you the one command to run in it.
# A conflict stops the cascade. Local only: it never fetches, pushes or
# deploys. Needs git 2.38+.
#
# DECIDE FIRST: a branch per environment is one deployment model; promoting one
# immutable artifact dev → uat → prod from a single main branch is another.
# If your CI promotes artifacts, do NOT arm this — the two would disagree about
# what is deployed where.

release
uat
main
